{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4839","published":"2026-11-11T12:26:43Z","modified":"2026-11-11T12:45:08.617327106Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-6862"],"summary":"efivar security update","details":"Some command line interface of the UEFI variables tools are offered by .\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in libefiboot, a component of efivar. The device path node parser in libefiboot fails to validate that each node&apos;s Length field is at least 4 bytes, which is the minimum size for an EFI (Extensible Firmware Interface) device path node header. A local user could exploit this vulnerability by providing a specially crafted device path node. This can lead to infinite recursion, causing stack exhaustion and a process crash, resulting in a denial of service (DoS).(CVE-2026-6862)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"efivar","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/efivar&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"38-9.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["efivar-38-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","efivar-debuginfo-38-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","efivar-debugsource-38-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","efivar-devel-38-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","efivar-libs-38-9.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["efivar-help-38-9.oe2403sp1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["efivar-38-9.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["efivar-38-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","efivar-debuginfo-38-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","efivar-debugsource-38-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","efivar-devel-38-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","efivar-libs-38-9.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-4839.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.openeuler.org/zh/security/security-bulletins/detail/?id=openEuler-SA-2026-4839"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-6862"}],"database_specific":{"severity":"Medium"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/A